{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"033aaa99019e7ddcc278635976cc4db3e7de01d0bfd3f316718f4cd3e709a222","digest":{"component_or_area":"review-bot receiver / uvicorn access logging","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","src/rebar/review_bot/config.py","tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_redaction.py","infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot","infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","infra/gerrit/webhooks.config","/webhook","/rerun","X-Rebar-Token","WEBHOOK_TOKEN","GERRIT_BOT_TOKEN","TokenRedactingFilter","install_access_log_redaction"],"problem_keywords":["credential exposure","plaintext logging","secrets in logs","query parameter authentication","journald leakage","access log security"],"propositions":["webhook and rerun endpoints accept authentication token as query parameter, which uvicorn logs in plaintext to journald on every request","the webhook token equals the review bot's Gerrit credential, so log exposure grants both webhook drive and Gerrit impersonation capabilities","access logs are grepped and shared in transcripts, so plaintext tokens can leak to external parties via incident investigation and log sharing","solution: move token from query string to X-Rebar-Token HTTP header (not logged by uvicorn access log) and install TokenRedactingFilter as backstop to redact any remaining token=value patterns while preserving route and status for observability","previously logged tokens must be rotated before or immediately after code fix lands, otherwise newly rotated credentials are exposed on first use"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787715977733967001,"uuid":"6c0a5a9a-b08c-4824-b0b4-ffec1a9de9e0"}